
# Canary receipts name a real account and window — evidence, not source.

# Phase-0 throwaway live gate (spec §3, 2026-08-30): .tok holds a live JWT and must
# never enter git; the .mjs beside it is throwaway too, left in place per the
# no-delete rule rather than removed.
.live-gate-phase0.*

# Location-binding throwaway live gate (spec §5, 2026-08-30): same pattern as the phase-0 gate
# above — a probe artifact left in place per the no-delete rule, never committed.
.live-gate-location.*
# Receipts left by the audit canary, which was removed with the audit server on 2026-09-16.
# The FILENAMES carry real location ids, so these must never be committed even though nothing
# produces new ones any more. The files themselves stay on disk — probe artefacts are left in
# place, named, for Xander.
audit-canary-receipt-*.json
